WEBVTT

1
00:49:12.970 --> 00:49:24.970
Jesus came to this earth to shake things up.

2
00:49:24.970 --> 00:49:31.970
He hung on the cross and said, behold, I make all things new.

3
00:49:31.970 --> 00:49:36.970
He didn't do that 2000 years ago and then it was finished.

4
00:49:37.970 --> 00:49:42.970
One of the core businesses of Jesus is to shake things up.

5
00:49:42.970 --> 00:49:46.970
And one of the things we do from a place of safety is to hold on to things.

6
00:49:46.970 --> 00:49:51.970
And that's why it's not always easy to let Jesus do His work in our lives.

7
00:49:51.970 --> 00:49:57.970
Because you let Him in and then He says, okay, but then we are going to approach things anew.

8
00:49:57.970 --> 00:50:00.970
And we are used to approaching things this way.

9
00:50:00.970 --> 00:50:03.970
And He says, yes, but I want to approach things again.

10
00:50:03.970 --> 00:50:05.970
Behold, I make all things new.

11
00:50:05.970 --> 00:50:08.970
So let's close our eyes. I just want this.

12
00:50:08.970 --> 00:50:13.970
When we have sung this, let's bring new wine.

13
00:50:13.970 --> 00:50:16.970
This is biblical language for the new wine.

14
00:50:16.970 --> 00:50:20.970
Wine was a harvest that came from grapes.

15
00:50:20.970 --> 00:50:24.970
And then, wine is the fullness of a certain fruit.

16
00:50:24.970 --> 00:50:28.970
The complete product, the best of the best, that is new wine.

17
00:50:28.970 --> 00:50:32.970
And then we say, we sing, Jesus, bring new wine out of me.

18
00:50:32.970 --> 00:50:37.970
Bring the full revelation of who God is, draw that out of me.

19
00:50:37.970 --> 00:50:40.970
Healing is in new wine.

20
00:50:40.970 --> 00:50:44.970
Receiving God's love is in new wine.

21
00:50:44.970 --> 00:50:48.970
No more old things, no more old theories, no more old perspectives,

22
00:50:48.970 --> 00:50:52.970
no more old ways of approaching things, no more the old way of thinking.

23
00:50:52.970 --> 00:50:55.970
And that's how I did it. And that's how I viewed relationships.

24
00:50:55.970 --> 00:50:57.970
And that's how I viewed myself.

25
00:50:57.970 --> 00:51:00.970
And for 39 years I lived this way.

26
00:51:00.970 --> 00:51:03.970
And I thought, fine, I'll just see.

27
00:51:03.970 --> 00:51:06.970
But when you sing, Lord, draw new wine out of me.

28
00:51:06.970 --> 00:51:09.970
Then Jesus says, behold, I make all things new.

29
00:51:09.970 --> 00:51:14.970
And this last week of this Open Relationships Month,

30
00:51:14.970 --> 00:51:17.970
I want to declare a blessing over Open Church,

31
00:51:17.970 --> 00:51:20.970
that Jesus draws new wine out of us.

32
00:51:20.970 --> 00:51:24.970
That He refreshes things, that He shakes things up.

33
00:51:24.970 --> 00:51:28.970
And I literally see in my mind, I see dust rising.

34
00:51:29.970 --> 00:51:32.970
And I see clutter rising in the name of Jesus.

35
00:51:32.970 --> 00:51:36.970
And if this is for you, and you know that clutter needs to be stirred up,

36
00:51:36.970 --> 00:51:38.970
so that the wheat can be separated from the chaff.

37
00:51:38.970 --> 00:51:41.970
And then, you know how that works, separating wheat from chaff?

38
00:51:41.970 --> 00:51:43.970
That's when they throw the grain into the air.

39
00:51:43.970 --> 00:51:47.970
And with the wind, everything that has no value can be blown away.

40
00:51:47.970 --> 00:51:48.970
He can take it away.

41
00:51:48.970 --> 00:51:52.970
Do you know who the best person for that is? His name is Jesus.

42
00:51:52.970 --> 00:51:55.970
He removes things that don't belong.

43
00:51:55.970 --> 00:51:57.970
And some things we have become accustomed to.

44
00:51:57.970 --> 00:52:00.970
And some things we have become attached to.

45
00:52:00.970 --> 00:52:04.970
While we actually know that they need to be taken away with the wind.

46
00:52:04.970 --> 00:52:07.970
I bless us as a church in the name of Jesus.

47
00:52:07.970 --> 00:52:11.970
That we make this last service of the Open about relationships.

48
00:52:11.970 --> 00:52:15.970
That through Jesus, we let Jesus work through us.

49
00:52:15.970 --> 00:52:18.970
During what we just sang, He was already working with us.

50
00:52:18.970 --> 00:52:20.970
During the Word shortly.

51
00:52:20.970 --> 00:52:24.970
That He can slice away, that He can remove things that don't belong.

52
00:52:24.970 --> 00:52:26.970
Like a two-edged sword.

53
00:52:26.970 --> 00:52:28.970
Today, things will be removed.

54
00:52:28.970 --> 00:52:32.970
Why? Because He wants to draw out new wine from us.

55
00:52:32.970 --> 00:52:35.970
And I bless us in Jesus' name.

56
00:52:35.970 --> 00:52:38.970
That God will do a new thing in your life.

57
00:52:38.970 --> 00:52:42.970
If you believe this and if you want this, say amen together.

58
00:52:42.970 --> 00:52:44.970
Amen, amen.

59
00:52:44.970 --> 00:52:46.970
Thank you again for being here.

60
00:52:46.970 --> 00:52:50.970
Give the person next to you an elbow.

61
00:52:50.970 --> 00:52:52.970
Or a kiss on the mouth.

62
00:52:52.970 --> 00:52:54.970
I don't like it.

63
00:52:56.970 --> 00:52:58.970
Yes, nice that you are here.

64
00:53:02.970 --> 00:53:04.970
Nice that you are here.

65
00:53:12.970 --> 00:53:14.970
It's great that everyone is here.

66
00:53:14.970 --> 00:53:16.970
Honey?

67
00:53:22.970 --> 00:53:24.970
Good morning.

68
00:53:32.970 --> 00:53:34.970
Good morning.

69
00:53:34.970 --> 00:53:36.970
Good morning Frans.

70
00:53:40.970 --> 00:53:42.970
Sometimes you feel more like a singer than when you speak.

71
00:53:42.970 --> 00:53:44.970
There are moments like that.

72
00:53:44.970 --> 00:53:46.970
You don't feel like you are talking.

73
00:53:46.970 --> 00:53:48.970
You feel like a singer.

74
00:53:48.970 --> 00:53:50.970
That's so funny.

75
00:53:52.970 --> 00:53:54.970
A part of the new is to sing to you instead of to speak to you.

76
00:54:00.970 --> 00:54:04.970
And a part of the new that God is doing is ...

77
00:54:04.970 --> 00:54:08.970
a part of the new is giving Him space to do His work in those moments.

78
00:54:08.970 --> 00:54:10.970
And not to pass by that too quickly.

79
00:54:23.970 --> 00:54:28.970
Worship is for Him, but in those moments when we worship Him, then He comes.

80
00:54:28.970 --> 00:54:33.970
And then He touches us and then He molds us and then He works with us.

81
00:54:43.970 --> 00:54:47.970
That is why it is such a powerful place to be in that worship.

82
00:54:52.970 --> 00:54:57.970
I think it is the most powerful place to be.

83
00:55:01.970 --> 00:55:07.970
I may share a word with us about giving.

84
00:55:10.970 --> 00:55:18.970
And I was thinking about how we are almost at the end of the year.

85
00:55:18.970 --> 00:55:21.970
It is true, the life of a mother makes the years go by faster.

86
00:55:21.970 --> 00:55:24.970
I don't know what it is, but it feels like it's almost Christmas again.

87
00:55:24.970 --> 00:55:25.970
This is strange.

88
00:55:32.970 --> 00:55:35.970
And at the beginning of this year, I started learning from Matthew.

89
00:55:35.970 --> 00:55:37.970
So I want to go back to Matthew.

90
00:55:37.970 --> 00:55:39.970
And I am going to the end of Matthew 7.

91
00:55:48.970 --> 00:55:53.970
And it is at the end of what Jesus teaches, the Sermon on the Mount.

92
00:55:53.970 --> 00:55:56.970
And He says at the end of everything He said.

93
00:55:56.970 --> 00:56:03.970
He says therefore everyone who hears these words of mine and puts them into practice.

94
00:56:04.970 --> 00:56:08.970
At the end of the Sermon on the Mount, Jesus says now then.

95
00:56:08.970 --> 00:56:14.970
Everyone who has heard these words and puts them to work, puts them into practice.

96
00:56:21.970 --> 00:56:25.970
That person is like a wise man who builds his house on a rock.

97
00:56:25.970 --> 00:56:36.970
The rain came down, the floods came up, and the storm beat against that house.

98
00:56:38.970 --> 00:56:40.970
But it did not fall.

99
00:56:43.970 --> 00:56:46.970
Because it had its foundation built on the rock.

100
00:56:55.970 --> 00:57:00.970
And then He turns it around and says listen if you have heard this but you do nothing with it.

101
00:57:00.970 --> 00:57:02.970
Then you will be blown away in the storm.

102
00:57:07.970 --> 00:57:12.970
So the key at the end of this teaching is that He says you must do it.

103
00:57:12.970 --> 00:57:16.970
He teaches from Matthew 5, 6, 7. He teaches about all this gold.

104
00:57:16.970 --> 00:57:19.970
He teaches about how you should live as people of the kingdom.

105
00:57:26.970 --> 00:57:32.970
But at the end of everything, it is not enough to be a lord.

106
00:57:38.970 --> 00:57:40.970
He says now go do it.

107
00:57:42.970 --> 00:57:44.970
Now get to work, do it.

108
00:57:48.970 --> 00:57:51.970
Now go do all these things you have heard me say.

109
00:57:55.970 --> 00:57:58.970
And we are busy with that our whole lives long.

110
00:58:02.970 --> 00:58:04.970
And part of that is giving.

111
00:58:04.970 --> 00:58:09.970
And we are going to give this morning, financially, but even more than that.

112
00:58:22.970 --> 00:58:25.970
But in the worship and now again.

113
00:58:25.970 --> 00:58:29.970
The offering we give is our whole life. It is everything.

114
00:58:30.970 --> 00:58:33.970
And money is just a part of that. Amen.

115
00:58:42.970 --> 00:58:44.970
But He asks for our everything.

116
00:58:44.970 --> 00:58:49.970
So what I would like to say this morning is give everything and also give a monetary offering.

117
00:58:54.970 --> 00:58:58.970
And if your faith and trust in that area is small, then give something small.

118
00:59:00.970 --> 00:59:04.970
For His influence on everything is much better than holding on to things.

119
00:59:05.970 --> 00:59:07.970
I warn you about that.

120
00:59:15.970 --> 00:59:22.970
And I am not only talking about money, but about peace, freedom, the ability to warn Him with a pure heart.

121
00:59:22.970 --> 00:59:25.970
These are some of the most valuable things that the Lord gives.

122
00:59:29.970 --> 00:59:33.970
That pure heart with which you can fully worship Him.

123
00:59:33.970 --> 00:59:36.970
What He has to offer you is so much more.

124
00:59:43.970 --> 00:59:48.970
It would be wonderful to just pass around buckets again this morning, but that is not possible.

125
00:59:49.970 --> 00:59:54.970
If you do not give monthly, but via the app, pick up your phone at this moment.

126
01:00:07.970 --> 01:00:12.970
And let us sow in the house of the Lord. Let us sow in what He is doing.

127
01:00:19.970 --> 01:00:24.970
2021 is almost over. And we started this year with the theme Get Ready.

128
01:00:24.970 --> 01:00:30.970
For the Lord is coming back and He wants us to live as a people who are ready for Him.

129
01:00:35.970 --> 01:00:38.970
Give or close your eyes, I am going to pray.

130
01:00:39.970 --> 01:00:41.970
Lord, we give you offerings.

131
01:00:43.970 --> 01:00:45.970
And we believe you at your word.

132
01:00:47.970 --> 01:00:49.970
And we want to build our lives on you.

133
01:00:53.970 --> 01:00:55.970
You are the only certainty.

134
01:00:58.970 --> 01:01:00.970
And we want to build our lives on you.

135
01:01:01.970 --> 01:01:03.970
You are the only certainty.

136
01:01:06.970 --> 01:01:08.970
You are the only secure place in the storm.

137
01:01:19.970 --> 01:01:23.970
So Lord, we give voluntarily and with joy and gladness to you.

138
01:01:27.970 --> 01:01:28.970
We love your kingdom.

139
01:01:31.970 --> 01:01:35.970
So I pray a blessing over each person and each family this morning.

140
01:01:37.970 --> 01:01:39.970
In Jesus' name. Amen.

141
01:01:56.970 --> 01:01:57.970
Sit down comfortably.

142
01:02:00.970 --> 01:02:01.970
Sit down comfortably.

143
01:02:06.970 --> 01:02:07.970
Yes.

144
01:02:12.970 --> 01:02:15.970
Lord, I pray that these words will come as healing.

145
01:02:18.970 --> 01:02:23.970
Even though they can sometimes be sharp, Lord, I just want to pray that these words will come as healing.

146
01:02:25.970 --> 01:02:26.970
Amen.

147
01:02:30.970 --> 01:02:43.970
What I want to teach today is, by no means, a quick fix for the things you may be going through.

148
01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:59.970
So don't think that I'm standing here from the podium throwing things out and saying if you're going through rough times or if you have pain in your heart, just do this and then it's solved.

149
01:03:00.970 --> 01:03:03.970
I understand very well that life can be very complex.

150
01:03:04.970 --> 01:03:11.970
And I understand very well that the pain we accumulate can sometimes be very painful.

151
01:03:12.970 --> 01:03:15.970
And that the way out is not always easy and then it's over.

152
01:03:16.970 --> 01:03:21.970
Even if it were so, we wouldn't have the concept of suffering with a long 'ij' in the world.

153
01:03:22.970 --> 01:03:25.970
Suffering can last a long time. Suffering can last a lifetime.

154
01:03:26.970 --> 01:03:32.970
But here is a Bible verse that we all know, both people from the church and people outside the church.

155
01:03:33.970 --> 01:03:37.970
Here is a Bible verse that almost everyone knows, Christian or not Christian.

156
01:03:38.970 --> 01:03:44.970
The words of Jesus echo throughout creation when he said, come to me if you are weary.

157
01:03:45.970 --> 01:03:49.970
Come to me if you are burdened by the weight of your problems.

158
01:03:50.970 --> 01:03:51.970
I will give you rest.

159
01:03:51.970 --> 01:04:00.970
In English, the translation in English says, come to me if you are weary.

160
01:04:01.970 --> 01:04:11.970
Weary is a kind of word that indicates fatigue over trying and doing.

161
01:04:12.970 --> 01:04:16.970
And you get tired of it. It is stretched out, it has become slack.

162
01:04:16.970 --> 01:04:22.970
It is stretched out, it has become slack. There was once energy in it, but it is starting to bend.

163
01:04:23.970 --> 01:04:25.970
Like an elastic band that once had resilience.

164
01:04:26.970 --> 01:04:32.970
But at a certain point, if you keep pulling on it for too long, it is no longer elastic, but long stretched out.

165
01:04:35.970 --> 01:04:39.970
And the words of Jesus echo over the earth.

166
01:04:40.970 --> 01:04:44.970
Come to me if you are weary and I will give you rest.

167
01:04:46.970 --> 01:04:52.970
And today, at the end of this Open Relationships month, I want to offer a few handles.

168
01:04:53.970 --> 01:04:57.970
That's it. A few handles to offer for people who are just having a hard time.

169
01:04:59.970 --> 01:05:02.970
And I have literally been carrying this around for weeks or months.

170
01:05:03.970 --> 01:05:07.970
And I have even written words about it in my personal reflections.

171
01:05:08.970 --> 01:05:11.970
Maybe prophetic, maybe very courageous.

172
01:05:11.970 --> 01:05:20.970
But I think it could still get even more intense with this world, because I read the Bible.

173
01:05:22.970 --> 01:05:27.970
And I see Jesus saying things that I read, for example, one of the things Jesus says.

174
01:05:28.970 --> 01:05:32.970
There will come a time when people will almost faint from fear.

175
01:05:33.970 --> 01:05:34.970
It is written in Matthew.

176
01:05:34.970 --> 01:05:40.970
And we are now in the COVID time and people are getting annoyed by it.

177
01:05:41.970 --> 01:05:44.970
Businesses, you have to close. What is going to happen now?

178
01:05:45.970 --> 01:05:51.970
Then another variant comes. Last night, the night before, another variant is coming. Everyone.

179
01:05:52.970 --> 01:05:54.970
And that makes you weary, right?

180
01:05:55.970 --> 01:05:59.970
And this is just one small example.

181
01:05:59.970 --> 01:06:06.970
That we are all globally tired of the COVID situation that is affecting the world.

182
01:06:07.970 --> 01:06:09.970
And that is just one small example.

183
01:06:10.970 --> 01:06:20.970
At the same time, I see so many more complex things happening around the world that make humanity extremely weary.

184
01:06:21.970 --> 01:06:25.970
And that has nothing to do with COVID, because we were already seeing those things happen with COVID.

185
01:06:25.970 --> 01:06:28.970
Where people go through life as a victim.

186
01:06:29.970 --> 01:06:38.970
Once again, the things I say today are not meant to pass judgment on people who feel like victims of the pain they are burdened with.

187
01:06:39.970 --> 01:06:42.970
And where people are tired of the things that have been done to them.

188
01:06:43.970 --> 01:06:48.970
I say this in no way to imply, oh you are a victim so that is not good.

189
01:06:49.970 --> 01:06:51.970
I say this to lead us all to wait for Jesus.

190
01:06:51.970 --> 01:06:53.970
So it is not a judgment, it is a pointing towards.

191
01:06:54.970 --> 01:06:58.970
We just sang, Lord take it out of me, shake things up out of me.

192
01:06:59.970 --> 01:07:00.970
And that is what this sermon is about.

193
01:07:01.970 --> 01:07:09.970
And when I was working on writing this sermon, I was once trying to write sort of bullet points.

194
01:07:10.970 --> 01:07:12.970
To write down topics that you can go through.

195
01:07:13.970 --> 01:07:15.970
But I try to do that as little as possible.

196
01:07:15.970 --> 01:07:18.970
Because of course, I know many people from this church and then it seems like I am saying something.

197
01:07:19.970 --> 01:07:21.970
Then it seems, oh yes, well he is talking to me.

198
01:07:22.970 --> 01:07:24.970
But I do not want anyone, I do not want anyone from you and you and you.

199
01:07:25.970 --> 01:07:27.970
I just want to take us all into the concept of being weary.

200
01:07:28.970 --> 01:07:31.970


201
01:07:32.970 --> 01:07:33.970
You get it?

202
01:07:36.970 --> 01:07:38.970
And again, I try to do it as little as possible.

203
01:07:38.970 --> 01:07:43.970
Because it could be that if I say something, you say, oh why are you saying that, it hurts so much, you know.

204
01:07:44.970 --> 01:07:46.970
But it is, come to Jesus.

205
01:07:49.970 --> 01:07:57.970
One of the things I will say is, for example, I see Cora sitting there and I think, Cora it is good that you are here.

206
01:07:58.970 --> 01:07:59.970
Come to Jesus, if you are weary.

207
01:07:59.970 --> 01:08:00.970
Do you understand what I mean?

208
01:08:01.970 --> 01:08:06.970
It is, you are weary from time, you have lost someone, it hurts and you are going through the mourning period.

209
01:08:07.970 --> 01:08:09.970
And you can become incredibly tired from that.

210
01:08:10.970 --> 01:08:11.970
And become annoyed by it.

211
01:08:12.970 --> 01:08:13.970
And you can throw in the towel.

212
01:08:14.970 --> 01:08:16.970
And you can think, you know what, I’m going, never mind.

213
01:08:17.970 --> 01:08:20.970
But instead Jesus says, if you are weary, come to Jesus, if you are weary.

214
01:08:21.970 --> 01:08:23.970
And you can become incredibly tired from that.

215
01:08:24.970 --> 01:08:25.970
And become annoyed by it.

216
01:08:25.970 --> 01:08:26.970
And you know what, I’m going, never mind.

217
01:08:27.970 --> 01:08:30.970
But instead Jesus says, if you are weary, you should come to me.

218
01:08:32.970 --> 01:08:34.970
And so I am just trying to offer a few handles.

219
01:08:35.970 --> 01:08:39.970
And I hope that for some people in this room, or if you are watching at home.

220
01:08:40.970 --> 01:08:45.970
I hope, maybe for you today it is the drop that makes the bucket overflow in the right way.

221
01:08:46.970 --> 01:08:51.970
That you say, okay, I have held on to struggles and I have held on to the things that have caused me pain.

222
01:08:51.970 --> 01:08:56.970
Today you hear the decisive words of encouragement and hope.

223
01:08:57.970 --> 01:08:58.970
And you can say to yourself, I am going for it.

224
01:08:59.970 --> 01:09:01.970
And maybe this is enough for a few people.

225
01:09:02.970 --> 01:09:03.970
This is how I want to present it.

226
01:09:06.970 --> 01:09:08.970
Come to me if you are weary.

227
01:09:09.970 --> 01:09:11.970
Come to me if you are bowed down under the weight of your problems.

228
01:09:12.970 --> 01:09:13.970
I will give you rest.

229
01:09:14.970 --> 01:09:17.970
These are the words that everyone knows so well.

230
01:09:17.970 --> 01:09:21.970
But I want to share exactly what Vanessa just mentioned in the offering talk.

231
01:09:22.970 --> 01:09:24.970
Exactly, this is what this sermon is about.

232
01:09:25.970 --> 01:09:26.970
Because I want to provide a bit of larger context.

233
01:09:27.970 --> 01:09:30.970
What does it actually mean to come to Jesus?

234
01:09:32.970 --> 01:09:33.970
